    "narrative": "Today\u2019s lineup is anchored by **Cal Raleigh** (78.02) and **Lawrence Butler** (74.61), our premier targets against favorable matchups. **Cal Raleigh** benefits from a distinct park factor boost and a weak opposing starter in Kay (xERA 5.28), while **Lawrence Butler** is our highest-upside play due to a substantial +13% dynamic platoon edge and a hitter-friendly environment bolstered by favorable wind. We are also leaning heavily into the high-score outings of **Will Smith** (71.42) and **Taylor Ward** (71.19); **Taylor Ward** specifically sees a massive +16% park adjustment, making him an essential start despite the moderate SP challenge posed by Civale.\n\nWe have prioritized speed and order position, which led to the difficult decision to bench **Luis Arraez** (54.21). While **Luis Arraez** remains a staple for batting average, he was edged out by **Geraldo Perdomo** (64.02), whose status as the leadoff hitter (+10% order bonus) and superior scoring profile against the RHP bridge forced him into the UTIL spot. Meanwhile, **Brendan Donovan** presents a tactical risk; while he is locked in at 58.97, his -15% platoon penalty against the LHP suggests his floor is volatile, though his leadoff duties keep him firmly in the mix.\n\nMonitor the status of **Cal Raleigh**, **Will Smith**, **Gavin Sheets**, **Tyler Freeman**, **Brendan Donovan**, **Masyn Winn**, **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, **Jung Hoo Lee**, and **Geraldo Perdomo** closely, as all remain \"Lineup Pending.\" Should any of these players drop in the batting order upon official announcement, their efficiency scores will regress significantly. Additionally, while **Daulton Varsho** (69.33) and **Jeremiah Jackson** (65.67) look strong, remain wary of the -2% penalty for **Daulton Varsho** when facing elite hold-threat catchers, a factor that could tighten the margin for stolen bases today.",
